sequenceDiagram
    title Panchanga Calculation - Data Flow

    participant Caller
    participant Names as PanchangaNames
    participant Tithi as Tithi
    participant Nak as Nakshatra
    participant Yoga as Yoga
    participant Karana as Karana
    participant Vara as Vara
    participant Next as NextEvent

    Note over Caller: Has sunLon, moonLon (tropical), moonSiderealLon (sidereal), jdUt

    Caller->>Tithi: calcTithi(sunLon, moonLon)
    Note over Tithi: raw = ((moonLon - sunLon) mod 360) / 12. number = floor(raw) + 1. Tropical lons only - ayanamsa cancels in difference
    Tithi-->>Caller: Tithi number, degreesElapsed, degreesRemaining

    Caller->>Nak: calcNakshatra(moonSiderealLon)
    Note over Nak: index = floor(normalized / 13.333). pada = 1-4 within nakshatra. Requires sidereal lon from Ashvini = 0
    Nak-->>Caller: Nakshatra index, name, pada, elapsed, remaining

    Caller->>Yoga: calcYoga(sunSiderealLon, moonSiderealLon)
    Note over Yoga: sum = (moon + sun) mod 360. index = floor(sum / 13.333). Requires sidereal lons
    Yoga-->>Caller: Yoga number, name, elapsed, remaining

    Caller->>Tithi: reuse Tithi result
    Caller->>Karana: calcKarana(sunLon, moonLon, tithi)
    Note over Karana: raw = ((moonLon - sunLon) mod 360) / 6. half = 0 or 1 based on tithi remaining. Depends on Tithi already computed
    Karana-->>Caller: Karana name, half, tithiIndex, elapsed, remaining

    Caller->>Vara: calcVara(jdUt)
    Note over Vara: index = floor(jdUt + 1.75) mod 7. The +1.75 shift sets vara boundary at 18:00 UT (Yamakoti sunrise)
    Vara-->>Caller: Vara index, name, abbreviation

    opt Next-event - find transition time
        Caller->>Next: nextTithi(jd, eclipticStateAt)
        Note over Next: Newton phase then bisection. Max 40 steps, tolerance 1e-8 days
        Next->>Tithi: calcTithi at each candidate JD
        Tithi-->>Next: Tithi
        Next-->>Caller: boundaryJD + nextTithi

        Caller->>Next: nextKarana(jd, eclipticStateAt)
        Next->>Tithi: calcTithi at candidate JD
        Tithi-->>Next: Tithi
        Next->>Karana: calcKarana with tithi
        Karana-->>Next: Karana
        Next-->>Caller: boundaryJD + nextKarana

        Caller->>Next: nextNakshatra(jd, moonSiderealStateAt)
        Note over Next: Moon-only root finding
        Next->>Nak: calcNakshatra at candidate JD
        Nak-->>Next: Nakshatra
        Next-->>Caller: boundaryJD + nextNakshatra

        Caller->>Next: nextYoga(jd, siderealStateAt)
        Note over Next: step = yogaRemaining / (sunSpeed + moonSpeed)
        Next->>Yoga: calcYoga at candidate JD
        Yoga-->>Next: Yoga
        Next-->>Caller: boundaryJD + nextYoga

        Caller->>Next: nextVara(jd, sunriseAt)
        Note over Next: Single call - no iteration. sunriseAt is caller-supplied callback
        Next->>Vara: calcVara(nextSunriseJD)
        Vara-->>Next: Vara
        Next-->>Caller: nextSunriseJD + nextVara
    end
